msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "Links a heritage entity to its Heritage Digital Twin (HDTNode), at ANY scale: a site, a building, a single unit (an inscription, US 100). HDT-O HP1 per ECHOES D7.1 §4.2. Two uses, told apart by the twin and not by the edge. (1) The STUDY's twin: from the HC1 the study is about (study\\_about\\_heritage) to the HDTNode marked data.hdto\\_role = 'twin' — one per graph, the chain EMStudio's applyHdto and s3dgraphy.hdto.declare\\_hdto write (HC1 -HP1-> HC2 -HP33-> HC16). (2) The twin of a PART (1.6.42): from a stratigraphic unit or an HC1 inside the graph to an HDTNode WITHOUT hdto\\_role — read as a list by s3dgraphy.hdto.read\\_part\\_twins (read\\_hdto()['parts']), each with the unit or entity it belongs to. No hierarchy is presumed: which part belongs to which whole is said by heritage\\_part\\_of (HC1 to HC1) and is\\_part\\_of (unit to unit), never inferred from the twins; HDT to HDT nesting is has\\_digital\\_twin\\_component. In RDF the edge is hdto:HP1\\_has\\_digital\\_twin whatever the source; its rdfs:domain (HC1) makes a unit with a twin a heritage entity as well, which is what having a twin means."
msgstr ""

